{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101338","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101338/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101338/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101338/events","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101338","id":2777590127,"node_id":"I_kwDOAO6SJc6ljqlv","number":101338,"title":"4.4.dev7 get_display_safe_area() with external monitor attached returning odd results","user":{"login":"SoloRobo","id":20973406,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTczNDA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20973406?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoloRobo","html_url":"https://github.com/SoloRobo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoloRobo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoloRobo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoloRobo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoloRobo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoloRobo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoloRobo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoloRobo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoloRobo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoloRobo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-01-09T11:41:31Z","updated_at":"2025-01-09T13:53:58Z","closed_at":"2025-01-09T13:01:41Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible on v4.4.dev7.official [46c8f8c5c]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.dev7 - Fedora Linux 41 (Workstation Edition) on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Single-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Radeon 780M (RADV GFX1103_R1) - AMD Ryzen 7 7840U w/ Radeon  780M Graphics (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using 2 monitors get_display_safe_area() appears to take into account the 2nd monitor as well as the monitor it is being displayed on.\n\nFor example I am using a laptop connected to a 1080p monitor.\n\nWhen the 2nd display position is this:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/787b1aa2-1acb-417e-9e60-9d0cde7ebd77)\n\nI get this result with get_display_safe_area():\n\n[P: (532, 64), S: (1920, 1016)]\n\nIf I change the location of the 2nd display to this:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a4f4bb9c-840b-41f0-9f46-6d812c4a8622)\n\n[P: (0, 64), S: (2880, 1856)]\n\nI doesn't feel this is correct, especially on a desktop OS with the monitors stacked vertically.\n\nI tried with both Wayland enabled and not with the same result.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nConnect an external monitor\nRun GDScript print(DisplayServer.get_display_safe_area())\nReview what is considered a safe area\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp_4-4-dev7.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18360894/mrp_4-4-dev7.zip)\n","closed_by":{"login":"SoloRobo","id":20973406,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTczNDA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20973406?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SoloRobo","html_url":"https://github.com/SoloRobo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/user